    {
      "name": "tm_transition_defect",
      "description": "Move a defect to its next lifecycle state. Legal moves: new→open/rejected/deferred, open→in_progress/rejected/deferred, in_progress→fixed/open/deferred, fixed→retest/reopened, retest→closed/reopened, reopened→in_progress/open/deferred, deferred→open, rejected→reopened, closed→reopened. Anything else returns ILLEGAL_TRANSITION and names the legal states. Every move is journalled. Moving to 'closed' or 'rejected' requires a resolution (fixed, wont_fix, duplicate, cannot_reproduce, not_a_bug).",
